WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:21.900
Another week sped by, and before Iris knew it, the last week of camp had arrived.

2
00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:28.165
Iris' tennis game had improved a bit more, giving her some new confidence.

3
00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:38.243
When she and Grace gathered the other girls together for a pep talk, they all agreed they were prepared to do whatever it took to crush the boys.

4
00:00:38.244 --> 00:00:42.647
Two of the more experienced tennis players looked worried.

5
00:00:42.648 --> 00:00:51.065
"I've been losing against Akira since junior camp," Natalie said, arms crossed. "I'm not sure I can beat him."

6
00:00:51.066 --> 00:00:57.660
"Same with me with Alex," Kaylee grumbled. "He's better than I am."

7
00:00:57.661 --> 00:01:07.048
"Well, I sure don't want to lose to my brother," Iris said firmly. "We've got to find a way to beat the boys."

8
00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:17.536
"Don't worry, girls," Grace said, waggling her eyebrows at them. "I have a strategy—we'll focus on our secret weapons."

9
00:01:17.537 --> 00:01:21.365
"Secret weapons?" Iris blinked.

10
00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:29.286
"Yes." Grace smiled. "You're one of them, Iris. You, Anna, and Risa."

11
00:01:29.287 --> 00:01:35.146
Iris exchanged glances with Anna and Risa. They looked unsure too.

12
00:01:35.147 --> 00:01:38.533
"What are you talking about?" Kaylee asked.

13
00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:42.753
Grace gestured to herself, along with Kaylee and Natalie.

14
00:01:42.754 --> 00:01:48.512
"Well, everyone's going to expect that the three of us are pretty good, right?"

15
00:01:48.513 --> 00:01:56.253
Kaylee and Natalie slowly nodded. Like Grace, they'd been attending tennis camp for a few years.

16
00:01:56.254 --> 00:02:04.593
Then Grace pointed to Iris, Anna, and Risa. "And no one will expect much from these three, right?"

17
00:02:04.594 --> 00:02:09.774
Iris' cheeks burned. "Hey," she said indignantly.

18
00:02:09.775 --> 00:02:14.502
"No offense," Grace said quickly. "It's just a fact."

19
00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:18.940
"So how does that make us secret weapons?" Risa asked.

20
00:02:18.942 --> 00:02:21.254
Grace's face lit up.

21
00:02:21.255 --> 00:02:25.146
"We are going to train you hard for the next three days.

22
00:02:25.147 --> 00:02:31.321
And we'll make sure each of you is ready, and that you have some tricks up your sleeve."

23
00:02:31.322 --> 00:02:33.908
"Tricks?" Iris said.

24
00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:39.218
"Yes," Grace said. "Who wants to learn one right now?"

25
00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:48.878
"I do!" Iris shouted even louder than the younger kids. And on the court next to theirs, Javier whipped his head around.

26
00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:54.035
"Shh," Grace said. "Secret weapon, remember?"

27
00:02:54.036 --> 00:02:57.897
"Sorry!" Iris pressed her lips together.

28
00:02:57.898 --> 00:03:07.049
"I'll whisper from now on." Still, she couldn't hold back a smile. The final matches were going to be great!

29
00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:17.535
The next afternoon at lunch, Jae stopped by the table where Iris was sitting with Grace and the other younger girls.

30
00:03:17.536 --> 00:03:26.443
"Hey, Iris, you've really improved your game!" Jae smiled widely at her. "I've been watching you play."

31
00:03:26.444 --> 00:03:33.999
He had? Iris grinned back. "Thanks. Grace has been helping me a lot."

32
00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:41.253
"Really?" He wrinkled his brow in surprise. "I'm sure you don't need help from her anymore.

33
00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:44.527
Maybe you can ask about coming back to the other group."

34
00:03:44.528 --> 00:03:49.507
He leaned in closer to Iris and bobbed his head toward the other table.

35
00:03:49.508 --> 00:04:01.575
"My group. You know, with kids our own age. Maybe you and I would even end up as doubles partners for the final matches."

36
00:04:01.576 --> 00:04:11.983
Iris sat up straighter in her seat. Jae was asking her to join his group! And it sounded like he actually wanted to be her partner!

37
00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:20.898
A smile fluttered across her face as she pictured the two of them playing together on the same side of the net while everyone watched.

38
00:04:20.899 --> 00:04:24.532
Then Iris snapped out of her pleasant daydream.

39
00:04:24.533 --> 00:04:33.220
Nearby, Javier had his head cocked to one side, as if he was straining to hear her conversation with Jae.

40
00:04:33.221 --> 00:04:41.633
And Javier wasn't the only one who seemed concerned. Grace had gone pale and silent over her turkey sandwich.

41
00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:49.474
"Um . . ." Iris bit her lip. "Thanks, Jae. It's probably not up to me, right?

42
00:04:49.475 --> 00:04:53.534
It's the counselors' decision. But I'll think it over."

43
00:04:53.535 --> 00:05:03.020
"Well, if it were me, I'd rather be with kids my own age." Jae shrugged. "But let me know what you decide."

44
00:05:03.021 --> 00:05:09.334
Without a backward glance, he headed over to Zoe's table.

45
00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:14.362
Iris saw Javier glare at her before turning back to his lunch.

46
00:05:14.363 --> 00:05:17.550
"What is he so mad about?" she thought.

47
00:05:17.552 --> 00:05:24.330
Grace let out a breath. "For a minute there I thought we were going to lose you."

48
00:05:24.331 --> 00:05:29.009
"You can't get rid of me that easily," Iris joked.

49
00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:35.326
Still, inside she was squirming. Jae had such a cute smile.

50
00:05:35.327 --> 00:05:40.358
And it would be fun to play doubles with him, if she didn't embarrass herself.

51
00:05:40.359 --> 00:05:46.321
If she said no to him, he'd go back to ignoring her all the time.

52
00:05:46.322 --> 00:05:57.149
Over the next couple of days, Iris tried to make up her mind as Grace, Kaylee, and Natalie showed Iris and the others everything they knew.

53
00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:05.475
Iris learned how to aim the ball to a specific area on the court and how to keep it in bounds.

54
00:06:05.476 --> 00:06:16.463
Best of all, Grace showed the beginners how to fake out their opponents by facing their bodies one way and then moving them in another.

55
00:06:16.464 --> 00:06:21.129
That made it hard for an opponent to predict where the ball would land.

56
00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:28.036
Iris studied the move. It wasn't so different from the soccer move that Papa had taught her.

57
00:06:28.037 --> 00:06:32.689
Iris gave it a try. Bam!

58
00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:39.424
"Wow!" Grace's face lit up. "That's it! You're a natural at that, Iris."

59
00:06:39.425 --> 00:06:43.587
"You're a natural at coaching, Grace," Iris told her.

60
00:06:43.588 --> 00:06:52.263
And it was true. Which was why Iris forced herself to walk over to Jae after lunch.

61
00:06:52.264 --> 00:06:57.610
"I'm going to stick with the younger kids' group," she said nervously.

62
00:06:57.611 --> 00:07:02.431
"Huh?" He looked surprised. "Are you sure about that?"

63
00:07:02.432 --> 00:07:06.096
Iris blinked and then nodded slowly.

64
00:07:06.097 --> 00:07:12.587
On her soccer teams, she had always been a good teammate. And that's what she was being now.

65
00:07:12.588 --> 00:07:14.518
"Thanks, but I'm sure."

66
00:07:14.519 --> 00:07:20.579
Jae shrugged. "Whatever," he said. "See you around."

67
00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:29.081
Back on the courts later, Iris heard Ben shouting instructions to Javier on how to improve his swing.

68
00:07:29.082 --> 00:07:39.076
Each time Javier's racket made contact with the ball, his face brightened.

69
00:07:39.077 --> 00:07:46.560
Even if the ball went out of bounds or crashed into the net, he seemed to be having fun.

70
00:07:46.561 --> 00:07:55.903
As though he was actually enjoying being outdoors and playing with real friends instead of imaginary ones in the computer.

71
00:07:55.904 --> 00:08:01.279
But each time Javier met Iris' gaze, he scowled at her.

72
00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:07.542
They'd barely spoken all week long, and this was beginning to bother Iris.

73
00:08:07.543 --> 00:08:12.547
On top of that, she could sense that something was bugging her twin.

74
00:08:12.548 --> 00:08:19.196
Still, with his unfriendly attitude, she wasn't about to ask him what was wrong.

75
00:08:19.197 --> 00:08:26.521
Only one thing between them seemed clear: there was no way she was going to let him beat her.

76
00:08:26.522 --> 00:08:39.512
Iris gripped her racket and turned her attention back to practice. She was in it to win it!
